Besides the additional Xilinx BSCANE2 related features, commit b5d1610 introduced some new logic to allow the dmi_jtag module to be reset with TMS cycling by entering the "TestLogicReset" state. However, the way this is implemented in dmi_jtag_tap.sv line 205 is extremely dangerous; the generated trst_no signal is prone to glitching and actually drives asynchronous resets within dmi_jtag.sv and dmi_cdc.sv















PR title: Functional Resets and Async Reset Glitch Prevention

Source: https://github.com/pulp-platform/riscv-dbg/pull/123

PR description:
This PR addresses issue #120 and introduces support for `dtmcs.dmihardreset`. The key changes separate asynchronous JTAG reset (controlled by `jtag_trst` signal) from synchronous functional resets triggered by JTAG TestLogicReset state or DTM reset CSR. The implementation uses new clearable CDC modules that synchronize clear requests across clock domains.

The author modified the DMI testbench to issue random resets during transactions and fixed a JTAG verification IP bug where `ir_select` wasn't reset during master reset.

